Alpine Linux (base distribution) and official Alpine Docker image
========================================================================

Shomsky Linux is based on Alpine Linux (https://alpinelinux.org/) and is
distributed as a Docker container built FROM the official Alpine Linux
Docker image (https://hub.docker.com/_/alpine), maintained in:

  https://github.com/alpinelinux/docker-alpine

docker-alpine is licensed under the MIT License:

  Copyright (c) 2019 Natanael Copa

The copyright notice and permission notice required by that MIT license
are retained in third_party/docker-alpine/ (verbatim LICENSE copy).

Alpine Linux itself is not a single-licensed project; the container image
aggregates packages under many licenses, including but not limited to:

  - musl libc — MIT
  - BusyBox — GPL-2.0
  - apk-tools — GPL-2.0
  - alpine-baselayout — GPL-2.0

Unmodified Alpine packages are redistributed as part of the container image.
Source for Alpine packages is available from:
  https://git.alpinelinux.org/
  https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/

"Alpine" and the Alpine Linux name and logo are trademarks of their
respective owners. Shomsky Linux is an independent project and is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the Alpine Linux project.

